      "writtenOn": "2024-02-05T16:06:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The old implementation of fuzzy scale factor matching transformed the sample radius by the transform and then compared the dimensions to the original. This changes it to just extract scale factors and compare to identity scale factor.\n\nHowever, the fuzzy threshold had to change from 0.1 to 0.2. Previously a scale factor of 0.8 applied to a 0.5 sample radius produced a new radius of 0.4, which was considered acceptable with the 0.1 threshold. To avoid changing when the decal shader kicks in, the threshold for the actual scale factor has to be 0.2 to let 0.8 be acceptable.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 721,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 723,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "b257f8b7a20725ebe347c29c6d8a38ddca74613b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
